{"date":"Friday 27 November 2026","updated":"12:00","sub":"Friday 27 November 2026 · GBP/USD. Watches the London killzone so you do not have to trade it: a map at 06:40, the leg and its equilibrium at 10:00, a scorecard at noon. It never calls a trade.","feed":"<article class=\"post\"><div class=\"time\">06:40<small>Morning map</small></div><div class=\"body\"><span class=\"tag\" style=\"--k:var(--blue)\">Morning map</span><h2>The nearest real draw is yesterday's low, 30 pips below.</h2><p class=\"lede\">Before London opens, this is where the resting orders are and how often price has gone to get them by noon.</p><div class=\"plan\"><header><strong>GBP/USD · 1.31257</strong><span class=\"side map\">DRAW MAP</span></header><div class=\"pools\"><div class=\"pool\"><div class=\"nm\">Yesterday's high<small>1.31242 · 1.5p below</small></div><div class=\"meter\"><i style=\"--p:41%\"></i></div><div class=\"odds\">41%</div></div><div class=\"pool\"><div class=\"nm\">Asia high<small>1.31312 · 5.5p above</small></div><div class=\"meter\"><i style=\"--p:44%\"></i></div><div class=\"odds\">44%</div></div><div class=\"pool\"><div class=\"nm\">Yesterday's low<small>1.30962 · 29.5p below</small></div><div class=\"meter\"><i style=\"--p:17%\"></i></div><div class=\"odds\">17%</div></div><div class=\"pool\"><div class=\"nm\">Asia low<small>1.30938 · 31.9p below</small></div><div class=\"meter\"><i style=\"--p:18%\"></i></div><div class=\"odds\">18%</div></div><div class=\"pool\"><div class=\"nm\">Last week's low<small>1.30757 · 50.0p below</small></div><div class=\"meter\"><i style=\"--p:1%\"></i></div><div class=\"odds\">1%</div></div></div></div><p>Nearest draw of 10 pips or more: GBP/USD previous-day low 1.30962 (about 30 pips below), EUR/USD previous-day high 1.09890 (about 12 pips above). Feed clock verification was weak this morning and no calendar was retrieved, so treat times as unverified.</p><p class=\"dim\">Watching only. Handover at 10:00.</p><section class=\"stage\" aria-label=\"Session chart\"><header><div><strong id=\"cPair\"></strong><small>15m · UK time</small></div><div class=\"views\" id=\"views\"></div></header>\n<svg class=\"chart\" id=\"chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 760 420\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Candlestick chart of the session with the desk's levels\"></svg><div class=\"pdk\" id=\"pdk\"></div><div class=\"scap\" id=\"cap\"></div></section></div></article>\n<article class=\"post\"><div class=\"time\">10:00<small>Handover</small></div><div class=\"body\"><span class=\"tag\" style=\"--k:var(--copper)\">Killzone handover</span><h2>A 15-pip leg up. Equilibrium is 1.31240.</h2><div class=\"plan\"><header><strong>GBP/USD</strong><span class=\"side map\">HANDOVER</span></header><dl><dt>Leg</dt><dd><span class=\"px \">1.31167</span> at 07:35 → <span class=\"px \">1.31313</span> at 09:50 · 14.6 pips up</dd><dt>Equilibrium</dt><dd><span class=\"px c\">1.31240</span> · 1.4 pips below price · returns by noon on <b>65%</b> of sessions</dd></dl></div><p>GBP/USD drifted up through the killzone, only just tagged its Asia high and sits on its equilibrium. EUR/USD ran below its Asia low into the previous-day low area and closed back above it, with its equilibrium about 9 pips overhead. The two pairs disagree, one at its Asia high and the other through its Asia low, which is SMT.</p></div></article>\n<article class=\"post\"><div class=\"time\">12:00<small>Scorecard</small></div><div class=\"body\"><span class=\"tag\" style=\"--k:var(--gold)\">Scorecard</span><h2>Equilibrium came back by noon.</h2><div class=\"plan\"><header><strong>GBP/USD</strong><span class=\"side res\">SCORECARD</span></header><dl><dt>Equilibrium 1.31240</dt><dd><span class=\"g\">Reached</span> at 10:00</dd><dt>Yesterday's high 1.31242</dt><dd><span class=\"g\">Reached</span> at 06:45</dd><dt>Asia high 1.31312</dt><dd><span class=\"g\">Reached</span> at 09:45</dd><dt>Yesterday's low 1.30962</dt><dd><span class=\"r\">Not reached</span></dd><dt>Trades called</dt><dd>None. This desk names levels; it does not call a side.</dd></dl></div><p>A quiet, split morning: GBP/USD ground slowly higher and revisited its killzone midpoint, while EUR/USD ran its Asia low and stalled below its midpoint, so neither pair reached the 06:40 nearest draw.</p></div></article>","week":"<section class=\"week\"><h3>Meridian 2 · week of 23 Nov · equilibrium reached by noon</h3><div class=\"wk\"><div class=\"\"><small>Mon</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Tue</small><b class=\"r\">no</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Wed</small><b class=\"g\">yes</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Thu</small><b class=\"g\">yes</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Fri</small><b class=\"g\">yes</b></div><div class=\"tot\"><small>Week</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div></div></section>","chart":{"pair":"GBP/USD","bars":[["00:00",1.31069,1.3108,1.30995,1.30997],["00:15",1.30998,1.31022,1.30991,1.30995],["00:30",1.30996,1.31007,1.30971,1.30995],["00:45",1.30989,1.30998,1.30938,1.30961],["01:00",1.30955,1.3102,1.30952,1.31017],["01:15",1.31014,1.31039,1.31008,1.31038],["01:30",1.31037,1.31088,1.31019,1.3106],["01:45",1.31064,1.31148,1.31064,1.31146],["02:00",1.31137,1.31208,1.31137,1.31201],["02:15",1.31199,1.31204,1.31168,1.31196],["02:30",1.31194,1.31274,1.31175,1.31265],["02:45",1.31252,1.31292,1.31244,1.31254],["03:00",1.31252,1.31312,1.3124,1.31271],["03:15",1.31275,1.31275,1.31216,1.31231],["03:30",1.31226,1.31248,1.31222,1.31231],["03:45",1.3123,1.3123,1.3117,1.31173],["04:00",1.31175,1.31184,1.31157,1.3117],["04:15",1.31167,1.31213,1.31163,1.31185],["04:30",1.31187,1.31189,1.31163,1.31174],["04:45",1.3117,1.31199,1.31158,1.31187],["05:00",1.31186,1.3123,1.31163,1.31229],["05:15",1.31225,1.31294,1.31211,1.31292],["05:30",1.31286,1.31309,1.3128,1.31297],["05:45",1.31293,1.31304,1.31242,1.31259],["06:00",1.31253,1.31276,1.31239,1.31267],["06:15",1.31262,1.31282,1.3124,1.31281],["06:30",1.31277,1.31283,1.31234,1.31241],["06:45",1.31239,1.31256,1.31215,1.31252],["07:00",1.3